00:30:04.840 --> 00:30:06.700
And he was like, oh, I didn't realize that.
然后他说，噢，我没意识到这一点。

852
00:30:06.820 --> 00:30:08.700
And I was like, yeah, my character is a vegetarian.
我就说，对啊，我的角色是素食主义者。

853
00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:12.240
And then Greg was like standing next to me and he was like, you know what?
然后格雷格当时就站在我旁边，他说，你知道吗？

854
00:30:12.420 --> 00:30:15.520
Anything you want to know about each of their characters, just go talk to them.
关于他们各自角色的任何问题，直接去问他们就行。

855
00:30:15.700 --> 00:30:16.640
They know their character.
他们很了解自己的角色。

856
00:30:16.640 --> 00:30:22.460
They know sort of like the canon of all, they've lived every episode and they know their individual
他们了解所有角色的背景设定，他们经历过每一集，而且他们非常清楚

857
00:30:22.460 --> 00:30:23.840
character story so well.
自己角色的故事线。

858
00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:25.820
I didn't know your character was a vegetarian.
我以前都不知道你的角色是素食主义者。

859
00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:27.220
When do we establish that?
我们是什么时候设定的？

860
00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:28.740
It's established early on.
很早就设定好了。

861
00:30:28.860 --> 00:30:31.880
And then like it's throughout, throughout all the years.
而且贯穿了整整这些年。

862
00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:35.820
Like at Diwali, I was like, I guess I'll just eat naan, whatever.
比如在排灯节那一集，我就想，好吧，我只能吃馕了，随便吧。

863
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:36.220
Naan.
馕。

864
00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:37.720
Like there's like a whole thing.
就像是有这么一回事。

865
00:30:38.040 --> 00:30:39.440
Oh, I'm going to look it up in the show Bible.
噢，我要去查查剧集设定集。

866
00:30:39.640 --> 00:30:39.780
Okay.
好的。

867
00:30:39.820 --> 00:30:40.720
Look it up in the show Bible.
去查查剧集设定集吧。

868
00:30:40.980 --> 00:30:44.960
Maybe we should, well, let's get back to this episode a little bit.
也许我们应该，好吧，让我们稍微回到这一集的内容上来。

869
00:30:44.960 --> 00:30:46.000
We got on a tangent.
我们扯远了。

870
00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:47.860
Oh, me and you on a tangent?
噢，我和你扯远了？

871
00:30:48.040 --> 00:30:48.800
Get out of town.
别开玩笑了。

872
00:30:48.820 --> 00:30:49.460
Hard to believe.
真让人难以置信。

873
00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:50.520
What are you even talking about?
你到底在说什么呀？

874
00:30:50.820 --> 00:30:51.120
All right.
好吧。

875
00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:55.820
So there's this scene early on where Pam and Michael are stuck in the office together.
所以，在这一集开头有个场景，帕姆和迈克尔被困在办公室里。

876
00:30:55.820 --> 00:30:57.940
And I remember I could not get through this scene.
我记得当时我怎么也演不下去这一场戏。

877
00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:03.500
There's this never ending drum roll where Michael wants me to announce who has a birthday coming up.
有个没完没了的敲桌子声，迈克尔想让我宣布接下来是谁过生日。

878
00:31:03.700 --> 00:31:06.060
And he also calls you his assistant in this.
而且他在戏里还管你叫他的助理。

879
00:31:06.060 --> 00:31:07.460
Which I think is hilarious.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

880
00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:12.040
Like he has such a grandiose view of his job and who he is.
他对自己工作和身份的看法真是太自大了。

881
00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:13.360
You are his assistant.
你是他的助理。

882
00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:16.060
You're not front reception for the whole company.
你不是整个公司的前台接待。

883
00:31:16.240 --> 00:31:17.400
You're Michael's assistant.
你是迈克尔的助理。

884
00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:18.100
His personal assistant.
他的私人助理。

885
00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:19.180
You're his personal assistant.
你是他的私人助理。

886
00:31:19.280 --> 00:31:19.980
Which is not true.
但这根本不是事实。

887
00:31:20.220 --> 00:31:23.820
And he does this never ending drum roll on the desk that was making me laugh.
他在桌子上敲个没完，把我逗得直笑。

888
00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:27.160
And he wants me to announce whose birthday is coming up.
他非要我宣布接下来是谁过生日。

889
00:31:27.240 --> 00:31:28.340
And I say, there's no birthdays.
我说，没有人生日。

890
00:31:28.660 --> 00:31:29.840
And he's like, well, next one.
他说，那下一个呢？

891
00:31:29.920 --> 00:31:30.780
Just who is it?
到底是谁？

892
00:31:30.940 --> 00:31:33.540
So then I say, well, Meredith's birthday is next month.
于是我说，好吧，梅雷迪思下个月过生日。

893
00:31:33.540 --> 00:31:37.820
And then I'm just giving him nothing in the scene.
在那场戏里我对他简直毫无反应。

894
00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:42.980
And he starts swooping his phone across my face to see if he can find signs of life.
然后他开始把电话在我脸前晃来晃去，想看看我还有没有活人的迹象。

895
00:31:43.600 --> 00:31:43.840
Yes.
没错。

896
00:31:44.280 --> 00:31:46.040
I cracked up.
我笑喷了。

897
00:31:46.140 --> 00:31:46.720
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

898
00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.980
He was so funny when he was doing that.
他做那个动作的时候真是太搞笑了。

899
00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:52.320
I just remember when I was rewatching this, I just remember losing it.
我记得重温这一集的时候，我记得自己当时笑得不行。

900
00:31:52.420 --> 00:31:58.220
But that's sort of where we set up that storyline is that we now have to throw a party for Meredith,
但也就是在那儿我们铺垫了那个剧情，就是我们现在得给梅雷迪思办个派对，

901
00:31:58.220 --> 00:31:59.860
whose birthday is next month.
下个月过生日的那位。

902
00:31:59.980 --> 00:32:01.440
This is like a real dork thing.
这听起来真像个书呆子才会做的事。

903
00:32:01.440 --> 00:32:06.100
But when I watch these early scenes of Michael's office, it looks so different over the years.
但当我看到迈克尔办公室这些早期的场景时，感觉这些年来变化好大。

904
00:32:06.260 --> 00:32:07.940
You know, like there's that shelf in the corner.
你知道，比如角落里那个架子。

905
00:32:08.180 --> 00:32:10.840
He doesn't have the tall standing shelf with two doors.
他当时还没有那个带两扇门的高立柜。

906
00:32:10.980 --> 00:32:12.060
It's a different lower shelf.
那是个不一样的矮架子。

907
00:32:12.240 --> 00:32:13.660
I don't know if you like look at all that.
我不知道你们会不会留意这些。

908
00:32:13.740 --> 00:32:14.280
And I'm like, oh.
我当时就想，噢。

909
00:32:14.820 --> 00:32:15.160
Wow.
哇。

910
00:32:15.520 --> 00:32:17.520
Like the furniture in his office keeps changing.
他办公室里的家具一直在变。

911
00:32:17.660 --> 00:32:19.760
This is a super nerdy thing for me to notice.
我能注意到这个真是超级书呆子行为。

912
00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:22.180
But I mean, I don't notice bobbleheads.
我是说，我都没注意到摇头娃娃。

913
00:32:22.380 --> 00:32:24.780
But if you're going to notice a major story point.
但如果你要留意一个重要的剧情点的话。

914
00:32:24.980 --> 00:32:27.360
If you're going to move a cabinet, I'm going to notice.
如果你要搬动一个柜子，我肯定会发现的。

915
00:32:27.360 --> 00:32:33.840
So the next big sort of plot point scene is Rain asking Jim if he wants to form an alliance.
接下来的一个重要剧情点是雷恩问吉姆想不想结盟。

916
00:32:34.040 --> 00:32:37.200
And this produced one of our inside joke lines.
这产生了一句我们的内部梗。

917
00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:40.560
He asks him if he wants to form an alliance.
他问他想不想结盟。

918
00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:42.220
And Jim pauses.
然后吉姆停顿了一下。

919
00:32:42.380 --> 00:32:44.880
And then he says, absolutely, I do.
接着他说，当然，我愿意。

920
00:32:45.280 --> 00:32:47.740
And we used to say that to each other on the set.
我们以前在片场经常对彼此说这句话。

921
00:32:47.900 --> 00:32:48.900
That used to be a thing.
那曾经是个流行语。

922
00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:50.400
Absolutely, I do.
当然，我愿意。

923
00:32:50.860 --> 00:32:52.600
I love this so much.
我太喜欢这个了。

924
00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:55.220
Because it's just like Jim finally gets to have fun at work.
因为这就像吉姆终于能在工作中找到乐趣了。

925
00:32:55.400 --> 00:32:57.940
This is like one of his favorite days, you would think, right?
你会觉得这算是他最喜欢的日子之一，对吧？

926
00:32:58.260 --> 00:33:00.420
Because otherwise, it's just the monotony of it all.
因为除此之外，工作全是枯燥乏味的。

927
00:33:00.560 --> 00:33:02.520
And Dwight does drive him crazy.
而且德怀特确实让他抓狂。

928
00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:05.300
And he talks about how crazy that Dwight makes him.
他谈到过德怀特让他有多抓狂。

929
00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:08.600
And he finally gets to like really mess with him at Dwight's invitation.
而现在他终于可以在德怀特的主动邀请下，好好捉弄他一番了。

930
00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:09.740
That is the beSt.
这简直太棒了。

931
00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:14.020
He has that talking head where he says, sometimes it's just handed to you.
他有个面对镜头的采访，说有时候机会就是送上门来的。

932
00:33:14.140 --> 00:33:16.860
I mean, you're thinking, how can I mess with this guy?
我是说，你本来还在想，我该怎么捉弄这家伙呢？

933
00:33:16.980 --> 00:33:19.400
And then here this wonderful gift comes.
然后这份美妙的礼物就送上门了。

934
00:33:19.400 --> 00:33:23.620
So after they decide to form the alliance, he says, don't tell anyone.
所以他们决定结盟后，他说，别告诉任何人。

935
00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:24.420
You can't tell anyone.
你不能告诉任何人。

936
00:33:24.540 --> 00:33:25.600
Jim's like, of course not.
吉姆说，当然不会。

937
00:33:25.780 --> 00:33:30.920
And then Jim immediately comes up to the reception desk and tells me that he's formed an alliance with Dwight.
结果吉姆转头就走到前台，告诉我他跟德怀特结盟了。

938
00:33:31.080 --> 00:33:34.520
And you see Dwight hovering in the background, listening in.
你可以看到德怀特在背景里徘徊，偷听着。

939
00:33:34.600 --> 00:33:37.380
And he wants to get Jim away from me.
他想把吉姆从我身边拉开。

940
00:33:37.400 --> 00:33:44.820
So he has this line where he's like, Jim, can I talk to you about the paper products?
所以他说了句台词，大概是，吉姆，我能跟你谈谈纸制品的事吗？

941
00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:48.520
So I listened to the DVD commentary of this.
我听了这段的DVD评论音轨。

942
00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:48.780
Yeah.
是啊。

943
00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:58.100
And I guess in that scene, they have a bunch of takes where Rain, every time, he would change the end of the line.
我猜在那场戏里，他们拍了很多条，雷恩每次都会改动台词的结尾。

944
00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:05.920
And I think it was Mike Schur said his favorite alt of that was, hey, Jim, can I talk to you about the...
我觉得是迈克·舒尔说他最喜欢的备选台词是，嘿，吉姆，我能跟你谈谈……

945
00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:10.240
He just like mumbled something that you couldn't even hear.
他嘟囔了一些你根本听不清的东西。

946
00:34:12.120 --> 00:34:13.080
I love that.
我太喜欢那个了。

947
00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:17.240
I also loved John Krasinski as Jim.
我也很喜欢饰演吉姆的约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

948
00:34:18.300 --> 00:34:22.640
You could just see John, I think because we know him, having so much fun.
你可以看出约翰玩得很开心，我想是因为我们了解他。

949
00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:27.620
When they go into the kitchen and Dwight's like, what are you doing?
当他们走进厨房，德怀特问，你在干什么？

950
00:34:27.620 --> 00:34:29.080
He's like, I'm working her.
他说，我在搞定她。

951
00:34:29.200 --> 00:34:30.540
He's like, I'm on this.
他当时就像是，这事儿我包了。

952
00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:35.660
Like, I just saw John, like our friend John, having so much fun in that moment.
我刚才看到约翰，就是我们的朋友约翰，在那一刻玩得特别开心。

953
00:34:35.660 --> 00:34:37.200
And it just made me smile.
这让我忍不住笑了出来。

954
00:34:37.560 --> 00:34:38.760
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

955
00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:44.300
The whole way that he is winding Dwight up in this episode.
他在这一集里捉弄德怀特的方式简直绝了。

956
00:34:44.300 --> 00:34:52.320
It happens again where he goes into the kitchen where he's supposed to be spying on Toby and Kevin who are having lunch.
后来又发生了一次，他走进厨房，本该去监视正在吃午饭的托比和凯文。

957
00:34:52.540 --> 00:34:52.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

958
00:34:52.820 --> 00:34:57.500
That conversation is the most ridiculous, like amazing, boring conversation.
那段对话简直荒谬到了极点，却又精彩得无聊。

959
00:34:57.500 --> 00:35:09.940
Yes, and that produced another most frequently quoted inside joke line on The Office, which is when they're talking about the bread and then John's take on that line, he says,
没错，那段对话贡献了《办公室》里最常被引用的内部梗之一，就是他们聊到面包的时候，以及约翰对那句台词的反应，他说，

960
00:35:10.180 --> 00:35:11.820
their bread is very good.
他们的面包非常好吃。

961
00:35:12.400 --> 00:35:13.340
Very good.
非常好吃。

962
00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:15.540
We would do that all the time.
我们以前经常那样说。

963
00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:17.540
And then here you are, the bread maker.
结果现在你成了那个做面包的人。

964
00:35:17.960 --> 00:35:19.060
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

965
00:35:19.220 --> 00:35:20.460
Full circle life moment.
人生真是个圆满的闭环。

966
00:35:20.660 --> 00:35:22.560
Guys, my bread is very good.
伙计们，我的面包非常好吃。

967
00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:34.780
Also, we cannot not talk about the fact of how eagerly Pam is to join in Jim's prank and becomes a huge participant, like, in pulling this prank on Dwight.
另外，我们不能不提帕姆是多么热衷于加入吉姆的恶作剧，她成了捉弄德怀特的主力军。

968
00:35:34.960 --> 00:35:35.580
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

969
00:35:35.740 --> 00:35:36.040
Yes.
是的。

970
00:35:36.200 --> 00:35:38.240
Well, this is their opportunity to spend time together.
毕竟这是他们共处的好机会。

971
00:35:38.440 --> 00:35:40.740
Any opportunity to team up with Jim.
任何能和吉姆组队的机会都不放过。

972
00:35:41.080 --> 00:35:46.560
I mean, in the deleted scene, we establish that the phone rings very infrequently.
我是说，在删减片段里，我们交代了办公室的电话很少响。

973
00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:47.240
Yeah.
没错。

974
00:35:52.760 --> 00:36:01.180
And Jim is just loving it and his talking head about, like, how brilliant you were that you just came up – Pam came up with that all on her own.
吉姆当时乐在其中，他在采访镜头里说，帕姆有多聪明，这一切都是她自己想出来的。

975
00:36:01.320 --> 00:36:04.180
Yeah, when I come up to his desk and I'm, like, all fraught with it.
对，当时我走到他桌前，表现得特别焦虑。

976
00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:05.360
Oh, I just don't know.
哦，我不知道该怎么办。

977
00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:10.380
Michael's told me so many things and I want to unload all these secrets, but he told me not to.
迈克尔告诉了我很多事，我想把这些秘密全倒出来，但他不让我说。

978
00:36:10.660 --> 00:36:13.760
And I'm doing that all so that Dwight can overhear it.
我这么做完全是为了让德怀特听到。

979
00:36:13.980 --> 00:36:14.820
Dwight's, like, jackpot.
德怀特当时心想，中大奖了。

980
00:36:15.440 --> 00:36:18.200
But Jim is just so enamored with Pam in the scene.
但吉姆在这一幕里真的对帕姆着迷极了。

981
00:36:18.320 --> 00:36:19.000
And you know what?
你知道吗？

982
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:20.460
I'm a jam fan, you guys.
我是“吉姆和帕姆”的粉丝，伙计们。

983
00:36:20.460 --> 00:36:21.100
I am.
我真的是。

984
00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:22.660
And I love their storyline.
我超爱他们的故事线。

985
00:36:22.660 --> 00:36:25.260
I was just, like, a total fan of them.
我当时完全就是他们的头号粉丝。

986
00:36:25.460 --> 00:36:29.300
And I remember, like, every little nugget they had together.
我记得他们在一起的每一个小细节。

987
00:36:29.300 --> 00:36:30.280
I was like, oh, my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

988
00:36:30.740 --> 00:36:32.720
And this is definitely one of those episodes.
这一集绝对是那种经典剧集之一。

989
00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:33.940
Should we take a break?
我们要休息一下吗？

990
00:36:34.140 --> 00:36:34.920
I don't know.
我不知道。

991
00:36:35.020 --> 00:36:35.900
Do you want to take a break?
你想休息一下吗？

992
00:36:36.080 --> 00:36:37.380
Please take us to a break.
请带我们进入休息时间吧。

993
00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:38.560
Oh, my God.
天哪。

994
00:36:47.960 --> 00:36:48.740
We're back.
我们回来了。

995
00:36:48.920 --> 00:36:49.120
Okay.
好的。

996
00:36:49.420 --> 00:36:49.660
All right.
行吧。

997
00:36:49.660 --> 00:36:58.220
So, another big part of this episode is Oscar baiting Michael into donating to his nephew's walk-a-thon charity.
那么，这一集的另一个重点是奥斯卡诱导迈克尔为他侄子的慈善步行筹款活动捐款。

998
00:36:58.420 --> 00:37:03.440
But Michael sort of not getting what a walk-a-thon is.
但迈克尔似乎没搞懂什么是步行筹款。

999
00:37:03.560 --> 00:37:03.700
No.
没错。

1000
00:37:03.700 --> 00:37:06.100
And so, he puts in this big bid.
所以，他报了一个大数目。

1001
00:37:06.100 --> 00:37:13.020
And this is an example, also, of the benefit of the documentary crew element of the show.
这也是本剧纪录片拍摄形式所带来优势的一个例子。

1002
00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:21.420
Because you can tell at first when Oscar walks into his office and asks him if he'll donate to his nephew's charity, he doesn't want to.
因为你可以看出来，起初当奥斯卡走进办公室问他是否愿意为他侄子的慈善活动捐款时，他其实是不想捐的。

1003
00:37:21.660 --> 00:37:25.000
Like, he would, if the cameras weren't there, he would probably say no.
如果当时没有摄像机在场，他很可能会拒绝。

1004
00:37:25.060 --> 00:37:25.560
Right, right.
没错，没错。

1005
00:37:25.680 --> 00:37:26.640
But he can't say no.
但他没法拒绝。

1006
00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:27.820
He wants to look like a good guy.
他想表现得像个好人。

1007
00:37:27.960 --> 00:37:29.260
He wants to look like a good guy.
他想表现得像个好人。

1008
00:37:29.260 --> 00:37:34.020
And so, then he goes over the top, and he donates $25.
所以他表现得有点过头了，直接捐了25美元。

1009
00:37:35.480 --> 00:37:42.400
And only later is it brought to his attention that it's $25 per mile.
直到后来他才意识到那是按英里计算的，每英里25美元。

1010
00:37:42.920 --> 00:37:43.660
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

1011
00:37:43.940 --> 00:37:48.980
And that realization happens in a great scene with Jim at the birthday party.
而那个意识到这一点的瞬间，出现在他和吉姆在生日派对上的那场精彩戏份里。

1012
00:37:48.980 --> 00:37:51.860
And there is just this long pause.
当时出现了一段很长的停顿。

1013
00:37:52.980 --> 00:37:54.000
I'll tell you what.
我跟你说。

1014
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:58.920
But Steve Carell is better than anyone at letting an emotion wash across his face.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在展现情绪流露于面部表情这方面，比任何人都强。

1015
00:37:58.960 --> 00:38:02.640
And you watch that emotion of like, oh, crap.
你可以看到他脸上那种“糟了”的表情。

1016
00:38:03.040 --> 00:38:05.120
Like, just like, oh, what'd I do?
就像是那种“天哪，我做了什么？”的表情。

1017
00:38:05.280 --> 00:38:06.560
Like, go across his face.
那种情绪在他脸上浮现出来。

1018
00:38:06.680 --> 00:38:09.480
And I feel like we see this again in Fun Run, right?
我觉得我们在《欢乐跑》那一集里又看到了这一幕，对吧？

1019
00:38:09.860 --> 00:38:14.120
Because he, like, signs up to do, like, so many miles, and he doesn't realize.
因为他报名参加了，却没意识到自己要跑那么多英里。

1020
00:38:14.660 --> 00:38:14.940
What?
什么？

1021
00:38:15.060 --> 00:38:18.660
Something about Michael does not understand the concept of a walk-a-thon.
迈克尔对慈善步行筹款这类活动的概念完全理解不了。

1022
00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:20.420
A walk-a-thon or anything like that.
步行筹款或者诸如此类的活动。

1023
00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:21.680
But, no, that is so good.
不过，这真的太搞笑了。

1024
00:38:21.680 --> 00:38:31.820
Well, I did – I added it up because in the episode, Michael, once he realizes it's per mile, he asks Oscar, like, hey, how strong is your nephew?
我算了一下，因为在剧中，迈克尔意识到是按英里计费后，他问奥斯卡：“嘿，你侄子体力怎么样？”

1025
00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:32.920
Like, is he in good shape?
就是说，他身体素质好吗？

1026
00:38:32.980 --> 00:38:34.260
And he did 18 miles.
结果他走了18英里。

1027
00:38:34.280 --> 00:38:34.760
He did 18 miles.
他走了18英里。

1028
00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:37.000
So, Michael has pledged $450.
所以，迈克尔承诺捐款450美元。

1029
00:38:37.820 --> 00:38:38.740
I did the math.
我算过了。

1030
00:38:38.860 --> 00:38:40.680
He thinks he's pledged $25.
他以为自己只捐了25美元。

1031
00:38:41.600 --> 00:38:43.860
But instead, he pledged $450.
但实际上，他承诺捐了450美元。

1032
00:38:44.320 --> 00:38:45.300
I also need to go back.
我还需要回过头来说一下。

1033
00:38:45.380 --> 00:38:48.000
I skipped something that I think is really a fun thing.
我漏掉了一个我觉得非常有趣的地方。

1034
00:38:49.180 --> 00:38:51.700
In the parking lot, there's a scene where Jim and Dwight –
在停车场，有一场戏是吉姆和德怀特——

1035
00:38:51.700 --> 00:38:52.840
Oh, I know what you're going to say.
噢，我知道你要说什么了。

1036
00:38:52.880 --> 00:38:53.480
What am I going to say?
我要说什么？

1037
00:38:53.660 --> 00:38:54.840
It was Phyllis' car.
那是菲利斯的车。

1038
00:38:54.940 --> 00:38:56.180
It was Phyllis' car.
那是菲利斯的车。

1039
00:38:56.480 --> 00:38:56.680
Yes.
没错。

1040
00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:02.980
Jim and Dwight are standing next to a car, and they are comparing notes about everybody in the office and what they've learned.
吉姆和德怀特站在一辆车旁，交流着他们对办公室里每个人的了解和发现。

1041
00:39:03.020 --> 00:39:05.760
And they're standing next to a car, and it's Phyllis' car.
他们站的那辆车，正是菲利斯的车。

1042
00:39:05.920 --> 00:39:06.180
Yes.
是的。

1043
00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:09.580
And Rain, as Dwight, keeps kicking the car.
雷恩饰演的德怀特一直在踢那辆车。

1044
00:39:09.720 --> 00:39:10.000
Yeah.
没错。

1045
00:39:10.780 --> 00:39:11.600
And Phyllis –
然后菲利斯——

1046
00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:12.420
She didn't care for it.
她对此很不高兴。

1047
00:39:12.420 --> 00:39:18.300
She was very nervous about it, and I guess at some point, she went up to Rain and said,
她对此感到非常紧张，我想在某个时刻，她走到雷恩面前说：

1048
00:39:18.360 --> 00:39:23.280
Listen, it's totally fine if you kick my car, but don't kick the car or the hubcap.
“听着，你踢我的车完全没问题，但别踢车身或者轮毂盖。”

1049
00:39:23.500 --> 00:39:24.200
Just the tire.
“只踢轮胎就行。”

1050
00:39:24.340 --> 00:39:24.940
Just the tire.
“只踢轮胎。”

1051
00:39:25.540 --> 00:39:28.280
We used to park our cars in that little parking lot.
我们以前常把车停在那个小停车场里。

1052
00:39:28.380 --> 00:39:28.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1053
00:39:28.740 --> 00:39:29.380
And then –
然后——

1054
00:39:29.380 --> 00:39:33.500
A lot of our real cars have appeared as cars in the show.
我们很多私家车都在剧里当过道具车。

1055
00:39:33.940 --> 00:39:36.640
And then they – in seasons later, they had us move our cars.
后来到了后面几季，他们让我们把车挪走。

1056
00:39:36.640 --> 00:39:39.720
I think maybe they realized there's, like, liability or something.
我想可能是他们意识到这有什么责任风险之类的吧。

1057
00:39:39.720 --> 00:39:43.820
I mean, so – but in those early days, those were our cars.
我是说，但在早期，那些确实是我们的车。

1058
00:39:44.020 --> 00:39:55.500
A very, very big element of this episode is the point where Dwight ends up in a box in the warehouse to spy.
这一集里一个非常非常重要的情节，就是德怀特为了偷听躲进仓库里的箱子里。

1059
00:39:55.920 --> 00:40:05.320
And more than any other question, when I put this out to fans for questions, the most questions that we got, the most frequently asked questions, were about this box.
当我向粉丝征集问题时，收到的问题里最多的、被问到次数最多的，就是关于这个箱子的。

1060
00:40:05.520 --> 00:40:05.720
Right.
没错。

1061
00:40:05.880 --> 00:40:07.640
How long was Rain in the box?
雷恩在箱子里待了多久？

1062
00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:09.400
How many takes did we do?
我们拍了多少条？

1063
00:40:09.860 --> 00:40:11.720
How many boxes did we use?
我们用了几个箱子？

1064
00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:19.820
One of the questions was there's a scene where Pam is on the phone doing a fake phone call, and the box kind of tips over.
其中一个问题是，有一场戏是帕姆在打电话假装通话，然后箱子翻倒了。

1065
00:40:20.020 --> 00:40:20.900
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等，等等。

1066
00:40:20.900 --> 00:40:21.780
And I laugh and run off.
然后我笑场跑开了。

1067
00:40:21.780 --> 00:40:22.860
Wait, I have a note card.
等等，我有个小卡片。

1068
00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:24.260
I have a note card about this.
我关于这个有个小卡片。

1069
00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:24.720
What is it?
是什么？

1070
00:40:24.760 --> 00:40:29.500
I want to – okay, I know you put it out to Twitter, but this is your BFF, so I get to –
我想——好吧，我知道你在推特上征集了问题，但我是你最好的朋友，所以我得——

1071
00:40:29.500 --> 00:40:30.280
Can I ask you first?
我能先问你吗？

1072
00:40:30.280 --> 00:40:30.800
You get the first question.
你拥有第一个提问权。

1073
00:40:31.260 --> 00:40:31.920
Jenna, question.
珍娜，提问吧。

1074
00:40:32.120 --> 00:40:32.620
Semi-colon.
分号。

1075
00:40:33.040 --> 00:40:35.360
Did you really break and laugh by the box?
你当时是真的笑场了吗？

1076
00:40:35.360 --> 00:40:39.040
I think you did because I know what happens to your shoulders when you really laugh.
我觉得你是真的笑了，因为我知道你真正大笑时肩膀会有什么反应。

1077
00:40:39.040 --> 00:40:40.320
This was the question.
这就是那个问题。

1078
00:40:40.540 --> 00:40:40.760
Ah!
啊！

1079
00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:43.040
This is the question that people want to know.
这就是大家想知道的问题。

1080
00:40:43.960 --> 00:40:45.420
I think I faked it.
我觉得我是装出来的。

1081
00:40:45.640 --> 00:40:46.080
What?
什么？

1082
00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:47.840
Yeah, I don't think I really broke.
是啊，我觉得我没真的笑场。

1083
00:40:48.040 --> 00:40:49.360
I don't want to believe that.
我不想相信那是装的。

1084
00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:49.880
I know.
我知道。

1085
00:40:50.160 --> 00:40:55.840
I think – because I remember shooting that scene, and I remember it was very technical.
我觉得——因为我记得拍那场戏的时候，记得那场戏技术要求很高。

1086
00:40:56.140 --> 00:40:56.380
Okay.
好吧。

1087
00:40:56.520 --> 00:41:00.940
So it was – I – it was happening over my shoulder.
所以当时——我——事情是在我肩膀后面发生的。

1088
00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:08.860
Stuff was happening over my shoulder, but there was a way where they wanted me to break at a certain moment, so it was kind of technical.
我身后在发生一些事，但他们希望我在某个特定时刻笑场，所以这有点技术性。

1089
00:41:09.140 --> 00:41:11.640
So you had to sort of get out of the way, and the box was tipping.
所以你得避开，然后箱子就翻了。

1090
00:41:11.640 --> 00:41:12.380
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

1091
00:41:12.620 --> 00:41:18.880
So I remember shooting it a number of times, and I remember thinking to myself, gosh, does this even look real?
所以我记得拍了好几次，我记得当时心里在想，天哪，这看起来真的自然吗？

1092
00:41:19.380 --> 00:41:24.020
Like, do I – it's a really – there are two things that I think are really hard to do when you're acting.
就像，我——我觉得演戏时有两件事真的很难。

1093
00:41:24.180 --> 00:41:25.160
One of them is cry.
其中之一是哭。

1094
00:41:25.400 --> 00:41:25.720
Right.
没错。

1095
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:27.120
But I think people would expect that.
但我想大家应该能预料到这一点。

1096
00:41:27.200 --> 00:41:29.380
But the other is to laugh convincingly.
但另一件难事是演得像真的在笑。

1097
00:41:29.480 --> 00:41:29.680
Yes.
是的。

1098
00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:32.620
You know who has the best fake laugh is Steve Carell.
你知道谁的假笑最厉害吗？是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

1099
00:41:32.980 --> 00:41:37.560
Steve Carell can do this fake laugh that is the most honest, genuine laugh.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔能演出的那种假笑，听起来是最真诚、最真实的笑声。

1100
00:41:37.560 --> 00:41:43.140
And every time he would do it, I would start to laugh, even though I knew it was a fake laugh.
每次他那样笑，我都会跟着笑起来，尽管我知道那是假笑。

1101
00:41:43.320 --> 00:41:44.500
It was so contagious.
那真的太有感染力了。

1102
00:41:44.820 --> 00:41:46.260
He is the best at it.
他在这方面是最棒的。

1103
00:41:46.400 --> 00:41:51.660
I find it's easier to cry than to fake laugh myself for acting.
我觉得演戏时哭比假笑要容易。

1104
00:41:51.660 --> 00:41:52.340
Fake laughing is very difficult.
假笑非常难。

1105
00:41:52.680 --> 00:41:53.080
It is.
确实。

1106
00:41:53.160 --> 00:42:00.840
The reason I think that I didn't really break is because I remember having anxiety over whether or not anyone was going to buy it.
我觉得我没笑场的原因是，我当时很担心别人会不会相信我的表演。

1107
00:42:01.220 --> 00:42:03.620
Jenna, I have a little something on my note card here.
珍娜，我笔记卡上写了点东西。

1108
00:42:03.780 --> 00:42:04.260
What is it?
是什么？

1109
00:42:04.280 --> 00:42:05.220
I have another note card.
我还有另一张笔记卡。

1110
00:42:05.220 --> 00:42:08.600
I wrote, this is the first time we see Daryl.
我写着，这是我们第一次见到达里尔。

1111
00:42:08.780 --> 00:42:09.180
Yes.
没错。

1112
00:42:09.680 --> 00:42:10.120
Yes.
是的。

1113
00:42:10.300 --> 00:42:14.840
When rain pops out of the box at the end, Daryl is down there.
当雷恩最后从盒子里跳出来时，达里尔就在下面。

1114
00:42:15.060 --> 00:42:15.440
Yes.
没错。

1115
00:42:15.480 --> 00:42:17.400
Now, he is not going to have a big scene.
他当时并没有什么重头戏。

1116
00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:20.680
We're not going to hear him speak until the next episode, which is basketball.
我们要到下一集篮球赛时才能听到他说话。

1117
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:21.320
Yes.
是的。

1118
00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:24.040
But that is the first time we see Daryl, so I was very excited.
但那是我们第一次见到达里尔，所以我当时非常兴奋。

1119
00:42:24.260 --> 00:42:24.620
I know.
我知道。

1120
00:42:24.760 --> 00:42:26.540
And look, my note card came in handy.
看，我的笔记卡派上用场了。

1121
00:42:26.920 --> 00:42:27.980
I love that about her.
我很喜欢她这一点。

1122
00:42:28.020 --> 00:42:31.340
I love how we plant seeds that grow later.
我喜欢我们埋下伏笔，让它们在后期发酵的方式。

1123
00:42:31.600 --> 00:42:31.820
Right.
没错。

1124
00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:41.560
That is a person who is going to be a major character on the show, but we introduce him just as a guy seeing rain come out of the box.
那个人后来会成为剧中的主要角色，但我们介绍他出场时，他只是个看着雷恩从盒子里出来的人。

1125
00:42:41.560 --> 00:42:47.940
Yeah, that is one of the things, and I know we say it over and over, and we will for the life of this podcaSt.
是啊，这就是其中一点，我知道我们已经说过很多次了，而且在整个播客期间我们还会一直说。

1126
00:42:48.160 --> 00:42:52.880
But one of the things I love about what Greg Daniels did is he starts in the middle.
但我喜欢格雷格·丹尼尔斯所做的一点是，他直接从故事中间切入。

1127
00:42:53.160 --> 00:42:55.420
He doesn't like spoon feed you information.
他不喜欢填鸭式地喂给你信息。

1128
00:42:55.880 --> 00:42:59.220
Just the way they design the show, you play catch up as an audience member.
正是这种剧集设计方式，让你作为观众得不断去追赶剧情。

1129
00:42:59.340 --> 00:43:01.700
You're just like a day in the life, and you're right in the middle.
就像是记录日常生活的一天，而你直接身处其中。

1130
00:43:01.860 --> 00:43:01.980
Yes.
没错。

1131
00:43:01.980 --> 00:43:02.860
And I love that.
我喜欢那样。

1132
00:43:03.040 --> 00:43:03.320
Yes.
是的。

1133
00:43:03.420 --> 00:43:04.100
I love that, too.
我也喜欢那样。

1134
00:43:04.420 --> 00:43:04.720
Okay.
好吧。

1135
00:43:04.720 --> 00:43:07.200
Here's a big confession about the box.
关于那个盒子，有个大秘密要坦白。

1136
00:43:07.440 --> 00:43:08.780
This is going to blow your mind.
这绝对会让你大吃一惊。

1137
00:43:08.960 --> 00:43:09.220
What?
什么？

1138
00:43:10.760 --> 00:43:13.780
Rain wasn't in the box most of the time.
大部分时间里，雷恩并不在盒子里。

1139
00:43:14.100 --> 00:43:15.260
Who was in the box?
那盒子里是谁？

1140
00:43:15.440 --> 00:43:16.540
Who was in the box?
盒子里是谁？

1141
00:43:16.620 --> 00:43:17.220
Who was in the box?
盒子里到底是谁？

1142
00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:19.440
Phil Shea, our props.
菲尔·谢伊，我们的道具师。

1143
00:43:19.460 --> 00:43:20.100
Prop guy.
道具小哥。

1144
00:43:20.260 --> 00:43:20.420
Yeah.
没错。

1145
00:43:20.660 --> 00:43:21.360
Phil Shea.
菲尔·谢伊。

1146
00:43:21.440 --> 00:43:21.640
Yeah.
是的。

1147
00:43:21.800 --> 00:43:23.260
Phil Shea is a very tall person.
菲尔·谢伊个子很高。

1148
00:43:23.540 --> 00:43:24.360
Yeah, well, so is Rain.
是啊，雷恩也是。

1149
00:43:24.620 --> 00:43:26.500
And he was in that box all the time.
他一直都在那个盒子里。

1150
00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:32.420
So most of the box acting was done by Phil Shea, of course, except for the end where Rain busts out.
所以大部分盒子里面的表演都是菲尔·谢伊完成的，当然，最后雷恩跳出来的那一刻除外。

1151
00:43:32.420 --> 00:43:37.440
So in that scene where I'm cracking up, Phil Shea was in the box.
在那场我笑场的戏里，菲尔·谢伊就在那个盒子里。

1152
00:43:37.560 --> 00:43:38.160
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1153
00:43:38.300 --> 00:43:39.400
You know what I think we should do, Angela?
安吉拉，你知道我觉得我们该做什么吗？

1154
00:43:39.660 --> 00:43:40.300
Tell me, Jenna.
告诉我，珍娜。

1155
00:43:40.520 --> 00:43:45.900
I think we should call Phil Shea and get him to answer all of our questions about the box.
我觉得我们应该给菲尔·谢伊打电话，让他回答我们关于那个盒子的所有问题。

1156
00:43:46.080 --> 00:43:47.160
What was it like in the box?
在盒子里是什么感觉？

1157
00:43:47.380 --> 00:43:49.400
Phil Shea, we are about to blow up your phone.
菲尔·谢伊，我们准备要打爆你的电话了。

1158
00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:53.030
Phil?
菲尔？

1159
00:43:53.370 --> 00:43:53.730
Yes.
在。

1160
00:43:53.950 --> 00:43:55.510
Phil Shea, it's Jenna and Angela.
菲尔·谢伊，我是珍娜和安吉拉。

1161
00:43:55.730 --> 00:43:56.370
Hi, Phil.
嗨，菲尔。

1162
00:43:57.370 --> 00:43:58.130
Oh, hey, guys.
噢，嘿，你们好。

1163
00:43:58.190 --> 00:43:58.590
How are you?
你好吗？

1164
00:43:58.790 --> 00:43:58.990
Good.
很好。

1165
00:43:58.990 --> 00:43:59.730
How are you?
你呢？

1166
00:44:00.070 --> 00:44:02.670
Thank you so much for letting us call and bug you.
非常感谢你让我们打电话来打扰你。

1167
00:44:02.670 --> 00:44:06.270
It's always a pleasure to help out Pam and Angela.
能帮到帕姆和安吉拉总是我的荣幸。

1168
00:44:06.730 --> 00:44:07.710
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1169
00:44:08.090 --> 00:44:09.210
Oh, Phil, thank you so much.
噢，菲尔，太感谢你了。

1170
00:44:09.250 --> 00:44:11.250
It's just so nice to hear your voice, I have to say.
我得说，听到你的声音真是太好了。

1171
00:44:11.250 --> 00:44:12.110
That's what I was thinking.
我也是这么想的。

1172
00:44:12.350 --> 00:44:14.230
I was like, gosh, it's so nice to hear your voice.
我当时就在想，天哪，听到你的声音真好。

1173
00:44:15.090 --> 00:44:17.450
Hey, what an experience we had for nine years, right?
嘿，我们那九年的经历真是太棒了，对吧？

1174
00:44:17.910 --> 00:44:18.270
Yes.
是的。

1175
00:44:18.570 --> 00:44:19.670
We were the luckieSt.
我们是最幸运的。

1176
00:44:19.830 --> 00:44:20.710
We were the luckieSt.
我们是最幸运的。

1177
00:44:21.030 --> 00:44:25.590
Well, if you have a second, Phil, can we ask you some questions from the Alliance episode?
那么，菲尔，如果你有空的话，我们可以问你一些关于《联盟》那一集的问题吗？

1178
00:44:26.750 --> 00:44:27.110
Absolutely.
当然可以。

1179
00:44:27.110 --> 00:44:36.970
So we opened up questions to the fans, and overwhelmingly, the thing people wanted to know about was the box that Rain gets into in the warehouse.
我们向粉丝征集了问题，大家最想知道的竟然是雷恩在仓库里钻进去的那个盒子。

1180
00:44:38.110 --> 00:44:39.150
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1181
00:44:39.370 --> 00:44:43.370
So they wanted to know how long he was in the box, everything about the box.
所以他们想知道他在盒子里待了多久，以及关于那个盒子的一切。

1182
00:44:43.530 --> 00:44:45.950
But, Phil, I know you were in the box.
但是，菲尔，我知道你当时在盒子里。

1183
00:44:46.190 --> 00:44:52.590
Rain only got in after all the shooing and the scooching and the sliding and then the tumbling was done.
雷恩是在所有的挪动、滑入、翻滚动作都做完之后才进去的。

1184
00:44:52.590 --> 00:44:55.030
Phil, you did all of that in the box?
菲尔，你在盒子里完成了所有那些动作？

1185
00:44:55.030 --> 00:44:57.570
You were the scoocher and the tumbler and all that?
你就是那个挪动和翻滚的人，还有其他那些动作？

1186
00:44:58.250 --> 00:44:59.050
I was.
是的，是我。

1187
00:44:59.390 --> 00:45:04.510
Apparently, Mr. Zabornak, our line producer, didn't think we had enough money to hire a stunt guy.
显然，我们的制片主任扎博纳克先生觉得我们没钱请替身演员。

1188
00:45:04.710 --> 00:45:07.230
So he assigned me to be in the box.
所以他指派我钻进盒子里。

1189
00:45:07.390 --> 00:45:10.770
And I remember I had to go out and buy my own elbow pads and knee pads.
我记得我还得自己去买护肘和护膝。

1190
00:45:11.310 --> 00:45:21.910
And then I had a loose walkie-talkie in there with me with Liz Ryan, who was the first AP, shouting out all of Brian Gordon, who was our director for that episode's command.
盒子里还有一个对讲机，我用它和第一助理制片人莉兹·瑞安保持联络，她负责传达那一集的导演布莱恩·戈登的指令。

1191
00:45:22.310 --> 00:45:23.950
I remember like it was yesterday.
我记得就像发生在昨天一样。

1192
00:45:24.210 --> 00:45:26.530
So, Phil, can you take me through it from the beginning?
那么，菲尔，你能从头给我讲讲吗？

1193
00:45:26.810 --> 00:45:30.810
You get a script, and it says this character has to be in a box.
你拿到剧本，上面写着这个角色必须待在一个盒子里。

1194
00:45:31.190 --> 00:45:32.310
So what do you do?
那你怎么做？

1195
00:45:32.370 --> 00:45:35.650
Because you're in charge of getting the box as the prop master.
因为作为道具师，你负责搞定这个盒子。

1196
00:45:35.830 --> 00:45:37.110
So where do you start?
那你从哪儿开始着手？

1197
00:45:37.110 --> 00:45:48.710
On that particular prop, I sought out Greg Daniels, and I said, do you see Rain sitting down squatting in the box, or is he kneeling down on his hands and knees?
关于那个特定的道具，我去找了格雷格·丹尼尔斯，我问他，你是想看到雷恩坐在盒子里蹲着，还是跪在盒子里手脚着地？

1198
00:45:48.850 --> 00:45:50.350
And he said, kneeling on his hands and knees.
他说，手脚着地跪着。

1199
00:45:50.490 --> 00:45:51.850
And Rain is tall.
而且雷恩个子很高。

1200
00:45:52.030 --> 00:45:52.990
Rain is tall, right?
雷恩个子很高，对吧？

1201
00:45:53.250 --> 00:45:54.330
And so are you, Phil.
你也是，菲尔。

1202
00:45:54.490 --> 00:45:55.190
You're very tall.
你个子很高。

1203
00:45:55.450 --> 00:45:55.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1204
00:45:56.150 --> 00:45:58.170
Yeah, Rain is, I think, 6'1 or 6'2.
是啊，雷恩我想大概有6英尺1或6英尺2。

1205
00:45:58.290 --> 00:46:00.190
I'm 6'1 if I blow dry my hair.
如果我用吹风机吹吹头发，我就有6英尺1了。

1206
00:46:01.170 --> 00:46:02.530
You do have great hair.
你的头发确实很棒。

1207
00:46:03.250 --> 00:46:05.610
You guys should know, Phil has an amazing head of hair.
你们应该知道，菲尔有一头令人惊叹的头发。

1208
00:46:05.690 --> 00:46:06.210
He really does.
他确实有。

1209
00:46:06.210 --> 00:46:06.970
Yes, this is true.
没错，这是真的。

1210
00:46:07.310 --> 00:46:07.870
I leased it.
我是租来的。

1211
00:46:07.950 --> 00:46:08.490
I leased it.
我是租来的。

1212
00:46:08.590 --> 00:46:09.670
It's a Hollywood fake hairdo.
这是好莱坞的假发型。

1213
00:46:09.830 --> 00:46:15.990
But I tracked Rain down, and I asked him to get on his hands and knees, and I was measuring for this box.
但我找到了雷恩，让他跪在地上，然后我量了一下这个箱子的尺寸。

1214
00:46:16.210 --> 00:46:19.710
Wait, you made Rain get on his hands and knees, and then you measured him?
等等，你让雷恩跪在地上，然后你量了他？

1215
00:46:19.890 --> 00:46:21.470
And you measured him to know how big it was?
你量他是为了知道它有多大？

1216
00:46:21.790 --> 00:46:22.910
That was season one.
那是第一季的事了。

1217
00:46:23.070 --> 00:46:24.170
Rain was willing to do anything.
雷恩当时什么都愿意做。

1218
00:46:24.370 --> 00:46:29.410
Then I went to a couple box cities around Southern California, and no one had a box close to that.
然后我去了南加州的好几家纸箱城，但没人有接近那个尺寸的箱子。

1219
00:46:29.410 --> 00:46:34.870
But then I went on to the Internet, and I looked at box manufacturers in Southern California.
后来我上网查了南加州的纸箱制造商。

1220
00:46:35.090 --> 00:46:40.750
I found a company in San Diego named Kent Landsberg.
我在圣地亚哥找到了一家叫肯特·兰兹伯格的公司。

1221
00:46:40.750 --> 00:46:46.990
And you have to understand, as prop people, we have a very short production time and lead time to get all these props.
你要明白，作为道具师，我们的制作时间和准备时间非常短，要搞定所有这些道具。

1222
00:46:47.150 --> 00:46:51.130
So I called this Kent Landsberg paper company and asked to speak to the manager.
所以我给这家肯特·兰兹伯格造纸公司打了电话，要求和经理通话。

1223
00:46:51.890 --> 00:46:55.670
And in a much more frenetic and hyper voice, I said, look, you've got to help me out.
我用一种更加狂热和亢奋的声音说，听着，你得帮帮我。

1224
00:46:55.770 --> 00:46:57.310
I have to have a custom box made.
我必须定做一个箱子。

1225
00:46:57.410 --> 00:47:00.890
I probably need about 100 of them, and they need to be this dimension.
我大概需要100个，而且它们必须是这个尺寸。

1226
00:47:01.170 --> 00:47:04.330
And San Diego is like three hours away, too.
而且圣地亚哥离那儿有三个小时车程呢。

1227
00:47:04.610 --> 00:47:06.510
Well, and also, that's such a good point.
嗯，而且，你说得太对了。

1228
00:47:06.550 --> 00:47:08.250
You didn't need one box.
你需要的不是一个箱子。

1229
00:47:08.470 --> 00:47:09.330
You needed 100.
你需要100个。

1230
00:47:09.530 --> 00:47:12.510
You needed 100 boxes because you didn't know how many takes we were going to do.
你需要100个箱子，因为你不知道我们要拍多少条。

1231
00:47:12.510 --> 00:47:18.310
And Brian Gordon, the director of this episode, ended up being notorious for doing tons of takes.
而那集导演布莱恩·戈登，后来以拍无数条而闻名。

1232
00:47:18.670 --> 00:47:21.770
So you were right to cover your bases and get 100.
所以你未雨绸缪准备100个是对的。

1233
00:47:22.170 --> 00:47:22.590
Yes.
是的。

1234
00:47:23.130 --> 00:47:23.490
Right.
没错。

1235
00:47:23.610 --> 00:47:26.070
And we shot that scene in the Dunder Mifflin warehouse.
我们是在邓德·米夫林仓库拍的那场戏。

1236
00:47:26.070 --> 00:47:28.070
We wanted to have some boxes on the shelves.
我们想在货架上放一些箱子。

1237
00:47:28.790 --> 00:47:29.530
Oh, right.
哦，对。

1238
00:47:29.570 --> 00:47:31.350
Just ones that he didn't bust out of.
就是那些他没钻出来的箱子。

1239
00:47:31.970 --> 00:47:32.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1240
00:47:32.390 --> 00:47:32.530
Right.
没错。

1241
00:47:32.550 --> 00:47:33.030
Of course.
当然。

1242
00:47:33.390 --> 00:47:34.650
It wasn't a prop box.
那不是道具箱。

1243
00:47:34.750 --> 00:47:35.690
It just appeared out of nowhere.
它就是凭空出现的。

1244
00:47:35.690 --> 00:47:38.910
So we had to give some legitimacy to where it originated from.
所以我们得让它的来源显得合理一些。

1245
00:47:39.010 --> 00:47:40.110
Look at all the detail.
看看这些细节。

1246
00:47:40.390 --> 00:47:41.310
Look at all the detail.
看看这些细节。

1247
00:47:41.310 --> 00:47:42.650
So how did you do it?
那你当时是怎么做的？

1248
00:47:42.750 --> 00:47:43.370
So how did you do it?
那你当时是怎么做的？

1249
00:47:43.430 --> 00:47:45.030
This guy said he would do it, no problem.
这家伙说他没问题，能做。

1250
00:47:45.230 --> 00:47:46.290
And then how did you get them?
那你后来是怎么拿到它们的？

1251
00:47:47.430 --> 00:47:48.510
Well, I talked to him.
嗯，我跟他谈过了。

1252
00:47:48.570 --> 00:47:50.510
He said the lead time is usually a month and a half.
他说交货周期通常是一个半月。

1253
00:47:50.610 --> 00:47:52.030
I said, we have four days.
我说，我们只有四天时间。

1254
00:47:52.070 --> 00:47:52.430
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1255
00:47:52.470 --> 00:47:54.250
I said, I need the boxes in four days.
我说，我需要在四天内拿到那些箱子。

1256
00:47:54.270 --> 00:47:55.590
And I said, it was for a TV show.
我还说，这是为了拍一部电视剧。

1257
00:47:55.710 --> 00:47:58.550
He said, it was for The Office, which is a remake of the British version.
他说，那是为了《办公室》，也就是英剧的翻拍版。

1258
00:47:58.690 --> 00:48:03.330
And he probably said, I'm sorry, I'm a huge fan of the British version, and I'm not interested in helping you.
他大概是说，抱歉，我是英剧的忠实粉丝，没兴趣帮你们。

1259
00:48:03.330 --> 00:48:03.890
I've never heard of your show.
我从没听说过你们的剧。

1260
00:48:05.590 --> 00:48:07.570
It's like you guys were listening into the phone call.
听起来就像你们在偷听那通电话一样。

1261
00:48:07.730 --> 00:48:08.530
Exactly what he said.
他确实就是这么说的。

1262
00:48:08.530 --> 00:48:11.650
No, no, he said he would be glad to make an exception for a TV show.
不，不，他说他很乐意为一部电视剧破例。

1263
00:48:11.790 --> 00:48:12.650
So he made it happen.
所以他促成了这件事。

1264
00:48:12.830 --> 00:48:17.090
We got the boxes delivered to Culver City, which is where we shot that episode in our first season.
我们把箱子运到了卡尔弗城，也就是我们第一季拍摄那一集的地方。

1265
00:48:17.250 --> 00:48:21.930
And then they put the graphics on the box, and we had them back two days before we were filming.
然后他们把图案印在箱子上，我们在拍摄前两天收到了货。

1266
00:48:21.930 --> 00:48:24.730
So we had it all done and ranged it in the box fine,
所以一切都准备好了，箱子也摆放妥当，

1267
00:48:24.730 --> 00:48:31.990
and then it was just about coordinating where the holes would be inserted by me when I'm inside the box with Dwight's Swiss Army knife.
剩下的就是协调好位置，好让我待在箱子里时，用德怀特的瑞士军刀戳出洞来。

1268
00:48:32.110 --> 00:48:33.990
And it was a great scene.
那是一场很棒的戏。

1269
00:48:34.230 --> 00:48:35.870
I mean, I remember we shot that down.
我是说，我记得我们拍了那场戏。

1270
00:48:35.990 --> 00:48:37.730
I think it was a Friday night we shot that scene.
我想我们是在周五晚上拍的那场戏。

1271
00:48:37.810 --> 00:48:38.590
But it was fun.
但很有趣。

1272
00:48:38.590 --> 00:48:39.530
Everybody was laughing.
大家都在笑。

1273
00:48:39.790 --> 00:48:41.710
The crew was always laughing on that show.
在那部剧里，剧组人员总是笑个不停。

1274
00:48:41.710 --> 00:48:45.530
And it was a great scene, and the fans love it so much.
那是一场很棒的戏，粉丝们也非常喜欢。

1275
00:48:45.570 --> 00:48:47.450
Oh, Phil, thank you so much.
噢，菲尔，太感谢你了。

1276
00:48:47.810 --> 00:48:52.870
I'm looking at a picture that I can email you that Michael Gallenberg gave me.
我正看着一张迈克尔·加伦伯格给我的照片，我可以发邮件给你。

1277
00:48:53.090 --> 00:48:57.790
I'm going to send you a picture as soon as we hang up of me getting ready to tape up the fist box.
我们挂断电话后，我马上给你发一张我准备封第一个箱子的照片。

1278
00:48:57.890 --> 00:49:03.910
And I don't know if you have the ability to post the picture on the podcast, but I'm going to take a picture.
我不知道你能不能把照片发到播客上，但我会拍一张。

1279
00:49:03.910 --> 00:49:05.310
We can put it on our website, maybe.
也许我们可以把它放到我们的网站上。

1280
00:49:05.670 --> 00:49:05.950
Yeah.
好啊。

1281
00:49:05.950 --> 00:49:11.450
Okay, I'll take a picture, and you can see by the expression on my face after about take 50.
好的，我会拍张照，你可以看看拍了大概50次之后，我脸上的表情。

1282
00:49:13.030 --> 00:49:14.810
You were like in a sweat lodge.
你当时就像在汗蒸房里一样。

1283
00:49:15.150 --> 00:49:17.050
Oh, Phil, thank you.
噢，菲尔，谢谢你。

1284
00:49:17.470 --> 00:49:22.450
But, Jenna, you were there, and you remember the last take when Brian Gordon said one more.
但是，珍娜，你当时也在场，你还记得最后一次拍摄时，布莱恩·戈登说再来一次吗？

1285
00:49:22.530 --> 00:49:25.450
I hope you remember this, where he had me do all this stuff.
我希望你还记得，他让我做了所有那些动作。

1286
00:49:25.570 --> 00:49:28.850
And then when I cut myself out of the box, everybody had went and hit.
然后当我把自己从箱子里切出来时，所有人都走了，躲了起来。

1287
00:49:29.270 --> 00:49:29.970
Oh, that's right.
噢，没错。

1288
00:49:29.990 --> 00:49:31.930
I came out into the warehouse.
我从箱子里出来，到了仓库里。

1289
00:49:32.430 --> 00:49:36.730
So he at least played a practical joke on me at the end to make me laugh, so that was pretty funny.
所以他最后至少跟我开了个恶作剧，让我笑了出来，那真的挺好笑的。

1290
00:49:36.750 --> 00:49:37.250
We did.
我们确实做了。

1291
00:49:37.250 --> 00:49:43.730
We left you in the box, and we pretended like we were still filming, and then you just were there for so long.
我们把你留在箱子里，假装还在拍摄，结果你在里面待了那么久。

1292
00:49:43.810 --> 00:49:44.930
That is horrible, you guys.
你们这群人太坏了。

1293
00:49:44.930 --> 00:49:46.170
That is kind of horrible.
这确实有点过分。

1294
00:49:46.350 --> 00:49:47.510
Why were we so mean?
我们当时为什么那么坏？

1295
00:49:47.770 --> 00:49:51.050
Phil, if I was there, Phil, I would have come up and said, Phil, get out.
菲尔，如果我在场的话，菲尔，我会走过去说，菲尔，出来吧。

1296
00:49:51.110 --> 00:49:51.590
They left.
他们都走了。

1297
